  "review_depth": "individual-compatibility",
  "decision": "The entire one-file hunk scopes the modern mat-mdc snack action button-color token to mat-unthemed, preventing that structural modern rule from overriding explicitly themed current buttons. It does not edit a legacy theme mixin. Keep the original16 legacy action/primary/accent/warn behavior; do not transplant this modern structural selector into the owned legacy Sass. Both exact peer npm floors already contain the modern structural selector; their component internals are not copied. The retained historical ordinary snack-bar-theme emits theme token values and does not embed this structural container rule. The actual original16-versus-packed style probes pass default and custom snack-container, action, and explicit primary action properties. This is a do-not-adopt decision for the add-on, not a claim to have executed or certified every current modern snack-bar interaction. The retained execution receipts apply to their recorded historical subjects. Current qualification additionally requires the complete current clean same-library packed106 and Sass invocations, exact minimum peer identities and the required owned default/custom light/dark style assertions with effective custom-theme and wrong-style controls; this source review alone qualifies no current execution.",
  "diff_sha256": "54a23a310fdb6c13ccca73846eb6c7e0e7798324bd308678e018e6a0152d02ba",
